{"name":"Evaporation","hex":"#d1d5d3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"evaporation","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The process of a liquid converting to the gaseous state.","The process in which all or a portion of liquid (in a container) is turned into vapour, in order to increase the concentration of solid matter in the mixture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evaporation"}],"entries":[{"title":"Evaporation","blocks":[{"text":"Evaporation is a type of vaporization that occurs on the surface of a liquid as it changes into the gas phase. A high concentration of the evaporating substance in the surrounding gas significantly slows down evaporation, such as when humidity affects rate of evaporation of water. When the molecules of the liquid collide, they transfer energy to each other based on how they collide. When a molecule near the surface absorbs enough energy to overcome the vapor pressure, it will escape and enter the surrounding air as a gas. When evaporation occurs, the energy removed from the vaporized liquid will reduce the temperature of the liquid, resulting in evaporative cooling."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/37/Watervapor_cup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evaporation","wikidata":"Q132814"},{"title":"Evaporation (deposition)","blocks":[{"text":"Evaporation is a common method of thin-film deposition. The source material is evaporated in a vacuum. The vacuum allows vapor particles to travel directly to the target object (substrate), where they condense back to a solid state. Evaporation is used in microfabrication, and to make macro-scale products such as metallized plastic film."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Thermal_evaporation.jpg/330px-Thermal_evaporation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evaporation_(deposition)","wikidata":"Q579501"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Condensation_droplets.jpg/500px-Condensation_droplets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Condensation_droplets.jpg/1280px-Condensation_droplets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Condensation_droplets.jpg/500px-Condensation_droplets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Droplets of water vapor in a pan.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACondensation_droplets.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Misty_road_after_rain.jpg/500px-Misty_road_after_rain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Misty_road_after_rain.jpg/1280px-Misty_road_after_rain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Misty_road_after_rain.jpg/500px-Misty_road_after_rain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rain evaporating after falling on hot pavement","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMisty_road_after_rain.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Scanning_tunneling_microscope_%28STM%29_250_nm_by_250_nm_image_of_one-atom-thick_silver_islands_grown_on_palladium_%28111%29_surface.png/500px-Scanning_tunneling_microscope_%28STM%29_250_nm_by_250_nm_image_of_one-atom-thick_silver_islands_grown_on_palladium_%28111%29_surface.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Scanning_tunneling_microscope_%28STM%29_250_nm_by_250_nm_image_of_one-atom-thick_silver_islands_grown_on_palladium_%28111%29_surface.png/500px-Scanning_tunneling_microscope_%28STM%29_250_nm_by_250_nm_image_of_one-atom-thick_silver_islands_grown_on_palladium_%28111%29_surface.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One-atom-thick islands of silver deposited on the (111) surface of palladium by thermal evaporation. The substrate, even though it received a mirror polish and vacuum annealing, appears as a series of terraces. Calibration of the coverage was achieved by tracking the time needed to complete a full monolayer using tunneling microscopy (STM) and from the emergence of quantum-well states characteristic of the silver film thickness in photoemission spectroscopy (ARPES). Image size is 250 nm by 250 nm.[2]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AScanning_tunneling_microscope_(STM)_250_nm_by_250_nm_image_of_one-atom-thick_silver_islands_grown_on_palladium_(111)_surface.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/%D0%A2%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%B8%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%BB%D1%8C_%D1%81_%D0%BC%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%B1%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%B9_%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%BE%D1%87%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B9.jpg/500px-%D0%A2%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%B8%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%BB%D1%8C_%D1%81_%D0%BC%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%B1%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%B9_%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%BE%D1%87%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/%D0%A2%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%B8%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%BB%D1%8C_%D1%81_%D0%BC%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%B1%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%B9_%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%BE%D1%87%D0%BA%D0%B